  "system_note": "Reviewed revenue line: billed revenue code 0191 (Skilled Nursing) for dates 2026-01-08 through 2026-01-21 (claim MR_SNF_07). Claim header documents the skilled care basis as: \"Skilled nursing for cardiac monitoring, diuretic titration, and daily weight monitoring with PT/OT reconditioning following acute decompensation of systolic CHF\" (Claim MR_SNF_07, claim row). Therapy treatment records show PT/OT sessions with 60 min PT + 45 min OT on multiple dates (e.g. 2026-01-08, 2026-01-09, 2026-01-12, 2026-01-13, 2026-01-14, 2026-01-15, 2026-01-16, 2026-01-19, 2026-01-20, 2026-01-21) (get_daily_services output). The dataset contains no payer-specific per-diem numeric thresholds (fallback to payer-agnostic reference guide), which only defines revenue code meanings and states the MDS \"supports but does not replace\" daily clinical documentation (Policy Documents/SNF/...SNF Level of Care - Definitions and Reference Guide.docx, positions 8 and 9). The per-diem-level extraction tool returned NULL level_determination_statement for every date in the range; the tool's metadata notes that a NULL means the facility did not document an explicit per-diem exception and that NULL alone \"does NOT by itself mean the day is unsupported\" (get_per_diem_level_notes output). However, several dates in the billed range have no therapy session rows in the daily services extract (notably 2026-01-10, 2026-01-11, 2026-01-17, 2026-01-18) and no nursing-specific progress notes were retrieved to document the daily skilled nursing interventions referenced in the claim header. Because the reviewer cannot confirm from the retrieved record that licensed skilled nursing services were documented on every billed date in the 01/08–01/21 range (the audit requires day-by-day support), and the dataset lacks payer-specific per-diem criteria and any nursing note evidence for the gap dates, there is insufficient evidence to determine that the billed 0191 level is fully supported for the entire date range. Recommendation: obtain the missing daily nursing notes/MDS entries or payer guideline numeric criteria to validate each billed date before issuing a per-diem downcoding or day-adjustment finding.",
